            <ArticleTitle>A microbubble of gas as an early indication of macular hole formation after vitrectomy surgery for retinal detachment repair.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>71-74</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5693/djo.02.2017.04.002</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a novel case of a 67-year-old man who developed a full-thickness macular hole in the presence of a microbubble after repair of rhegmatogenous retinal detachment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
